{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784147409,"nonce":"yB3hE7GLJNEzMesVmqb+7skvPQ8=","title":"Make manual/API launch a **repo+ref-aware trigger** (ADR-0043 \"World B\"), reusing the webhook machinery instead of the repo-less inline `POST /v1/runs` shortcut. This is what lets a manually-dispatched *deploy* inherit Environment governance.","message":"Scope, end-to-end:\n- **`on: manual` opt-in** — a pipeline is manually dispatchable iff its `on:` includes `manual`; `on: api` is the programmatic sibling supplying the same declared parameters. This makes the pipeline→trigger mapping explicit and discoverable.\n- **Dispatch path** — a new dispatch entrypoint takes `{ repo, ref, pipeline, params }` and routes through the same read-at-ref/compile/admission flow the webhook uses (`list_dir_at_ref` → `read_file_at_ref` → transitive lib pre-fetch → pure compile), rather than accepting an inline IR. It then `coerce`+`validate`s params fail-closed (slice 1's shared path), freezes them on the Run, and creates the run.\n- **Resolve ref → SHA at dispatch** — the dispatched run pins the concrete commit SHA (reproducible, self-describing per ADR-0022). Manual/API `Event`s carry the repo + resolved ref so `trigger_run_from_event` (or its dispatch sibling) no longer treats them as repo-less.\n- **Governance intact** — a dispatched deploy (`environment:` pipeline) hits admission → the Environment's protection rules (approvers, wait timer, allowed-refs, concurrency) identically to a webhook deploy. Params supplied ≠ approval granted; the dispatch ref must satisfy allowed-refs, fail-closed. Manual dispatch is a trigger, never authority (gate-bypass authority is a deferred future ADR).\n- Inline `POST /v1/runs` remains as the baseline-only ad-hoc/dogfood escape hatch.\n\n\n- [ ] A pipeline with `on: manual` (and/or `on: api`) is dispatchable by repo+ref+name; one without a matching trigger is rejected.\n- [ ] Dispatch reads config at the ref, compiles (including `invoke:` lib pre-fetch), and creates a run — no inline IR accepted on this path.\n- [ ] The dispatch resolves ref → a concrete SHA and records it on the Run.\n- [ ] Params are `coerce`+`validate`d fail-closed at dispatch; a required-missing / invalid param rejects the dispatch with a structured per-param error and creates no run.\n- [ ] A dispatched deploy suspends on the Environment approval gate and honours allowed-refs (fail-closed) — verified by a test that a disallowed ref is rejected and an allowed one suspends pending approval.\n- [ ] Manual/API `Event`s carry repo + ref and are no longer short-circuited as repo-less.\n\n\n- ba20e88 (slice 1)","files":null}]}